// --- build adjacency list ---
This function takes a list of edges and the number of nodes to build an adjacency list representation of the graph. Each node points to a list of its neighbors.

// --- BFS traversal ---
BFS is used to traverse the graph starting from a given node. It uses a queue to explore all nodes at the present depth prior to moving on to nodes at the next depth level.

// --- DFS traversal ---
DFS explores as far as possible along each branch before backtracking. It uses recursion to visit nodes and their neighbors.

